# FY26 Emissions Data
# Emissions accounting for Scope 3 reduction planning (tCO2e). data_quality: measured = from supplier or meter data, estimated = modelled or spend-based

scope,category,tonnes_co2e,data_quality,source_allocation
Scope1,Direct,5000,measured,Owned facilities and vehicles
Scope2,Indirect Power,15000,measured,Purchased electricity
Scope3,Purchased goods and materials,180000,estimated,Suppliers and materials (spend-based)
Scope3,Transportation,45000,estimated,Inbound and outbound freight
Scope3,Use of Products,50000,estimated,Customer use phase

SUMMARY:
Total emissions: 295,000 tCO2e. Scope 3 total: 275,000 tCO2e (93% of the total).

LEVER INPUTS:
Air freight: 12,000 tCO2e a year from 8,000 tonnes of goods flown (measured volumes, emissions estimated). Sea freight alternative carries about 7,500 tonnes with a 4-week longer lead time.
Shifting 30% of air freight to sea: about 2,400 tCO2e a year saved (estimate, net of sea emissions).
Recycled polyester across basics: about 35,000 tCO2e a year at full conversion (estimate, supplier-average factors, not verified).
Top 20 suppliers: 110,000 tCO2e of the purchased goods and materials figure (estimate). About 35% of that, 38,500 tCO2e, is purchased electricity that renewable electricity would remove (estimate).
